<header class="phead"><div class="wrap"><h1>Tally<span class="h1-sub">Reconciliation</span></h1><p>Tally does the reconciliation every day so that close is a review rather than an excavation. The number that matters is not how fast it reconciles, it is how few breaks are still unexplained on day one of close.</p></div></header><section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="split"><div><h2>How Tally does the work.</h2><p class="intro">Balances sub-ledgers to the GL line by line and hands back a clean exception list instead of a spreadsheet nobody wants to open.</p><ol class="runbook"><li><span class="n">01</span><div><h4>Reconciles daily, not monthly</h4><p>Sub-ledger to GL, bank to cash, intercompany to intercompany, matched line by line every day. A break found on the day it happens is a five-minute question to someone who still remembers. The same break found at close is an investigation.</p></div></li><li><span class="n">02</span><div><h4>Matches on substance, not just reference</h4><p>Exact reference matches are the easy half. Tally also matches on amount-and-date proximity, partial settlements against one invoice, and payments that arrived netted across several, the cases that normally get manually unpicked.</p></div></li><li><span class="n">03</span><div><h4>Ages every break</h4><p>Each unmatched item carries its age, its size and its history. A three-day-old break is noise; the same break at forty days is a control problem, and it is reported as one.</p></div></li><li><span class="n">04</span><div><h4>Drafts the variance commentary</h4><p>Movement against prior period and against budget, with a written explanation drawn from the underlying transactions. The controller edits a draft instead of starting from a blank cell.</p></div></li><li><span class="n">05</span><div><h4>Proposes accruals with their support</h4><p>Where goods are received and not invoiced, or a service period straddles the cut-off, Tally proposes the accrual and attaches the documents it based it on. The support is in the proposal, not requested afterwards.</p></div></li></ol></div><aside><div class="panel"><p class="h">Connects to</p><ul><li>SAP HANA</li><li>NetSuite</li><li>Dynamics 365</li><li>Bank statements</li><li>Sub-ledgers</li></ul></div><div class="panel"><p class="h">What you get back</p><ul><li>Daily reconciliation status by account</li><li>Aged break list with size and history</li><li>Drafted variance commentary</li><li>Accrual proposals with support attached</li></ul></div><div class="panel"><p class="h">Deployed in</p><ul><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/industries/financial-services' ) ); ?>">Financial services</a></li><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/industries/venture-and-private-capital' ) ); ?>">Venture &amp; private capital</a></li></ul></div></aside></div><p class="gate"><strong>Where Tally stops.</strong> Tally proposes journals. It does not post them. Every entry that touches the GL is approved by a person first.</p></div></section><section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="bespoke"><h3>Your agents are built around your organization.</h3><p>The way you price, route, approve and escalate is years of accumulated judgment, and it's a real advantage. It belongs to you and it stays with you, we're not asking you to hand over your playbook or fit yourself into someone else's template. We start from how your business already works, encode that logic into agents built for your environment, and leave you with an operation that runs faster with exactly the things that make you good at it still intact.</p></div><p class="more"><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/work' ) ); ?>">See all six agents →</a></p></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="wrap"><h2>Bring us one workflow.</h2><p>Thirty minutes, no deck. Pick the process that costs you most in people, errors or delay, and we'll pressure-test whether an agent is genuinely the right answer for it.</p><ul class="cta-list"><li>An honest read on whether that workflow is a good agent candidate</li><li>What the first deployment would involve, and roughly what it costs</li><li>An honest answer if the sequencing is wrong and you should fix something else first</li></ul><a class="btn btn-lg" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/contact' ) ); ?>">Book a discovery call</a></div></section>
